+Each item is placed in one cell, chosen from its size and its center: the
+smallest cell at least as big as the item, among those containing its
+center. Because cells are tested with a box twice their size (they are
+"loose"), the item always fits in that box. Placing an item takes the same
+few steps however many items there are, and moving an item only changes the
+tree if its center moves to another cell or it changes size a lot.
+
+Items outside the region are kept in a separate list and tested one by one,
+so they are still found. The region is set with SetRegion, ideally before
+any items are added.
+
