+This class only describes what a render tree does. Its actions are blank.
+Use one of the kinds of render tree, which can be swapped for one another
+because they all have these actions:
+
+- DynamicVolumeRenderTree, a tree of boxes that fit around the items, like
+  the one physics uses. A good choice for most scenes, and for scenes whose
+  items are spread unevenly or move a lot.
+- QuadTree3D, which divides the ground into squares. A good choice for a
+  scene that is mostly flat and spread out, such as terrain and the things
+  on it.
+- Octree, which divides space into cubes. A good choice for a scene spread
+  out in every direction, such as space or a tall city.
+
+Each answer is added to an Array the caller passes in. The caller empties the
+array when it starts a new frame or pass, with Empty(false) so the array
+keeps its storage and no new one is made. The answers include hidden items;
+the caller can leave them out with IsShowing or IsShowingWithParents.
